{
 "description": "Documentaries built on an investigation: documents, records, timelines and the gap between what was said and what the evidence shows. Every claim carries its basis; an allegation is narrated as an allegation until a record settles it.",
 "entity_handling": [
  "An allegation is never narrated as a verdict: accusations are attributed to who made them, and findings to the body that recorded them.",
  "People under investigation are given their recorded response — a denial, a refusal to comment, a court outcome — wherever the sources carry one; absence of a response is stated, not filled in.",
  "Documents are shown only when genuinely retrieved with recorded provenance; a document the production does not hold is described, never fabricated on screen.",
  "Vulnerable sources and whistleblowers are not identified beyond what the retrieved sources themselves publish."
 ],
